= Grassroots Organizing

Movements win elections that candidates cannot. Whom should we organize?

- @indivisible_model: Neighborhood resistance groups
- @labor_community: Labor and community coalition
- @faith_and_veterans: Faith and veterans outreach
- @easy_discard

@indivisible_model
on-arrival: civic_strength += 400; dem_enthusiasm += 0.6; radicalization -= 0; progressive_strength += 2; month_actions += 1

Thousands of volunteer-run local chapters sprout up, trained in nonviolent tactics.

@labor_community
on-arrival: civic_strength += 250; labor_strength += 3; labor_relation += 5; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); minority_dem += 2*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

Unions and community groups share staff, phone banks, and trust.

@faith_and_veterans
on-arrival: civic_strength += 200; rural_dem += 2*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); moderate_strength += 2; month_actions += 1

Pastors and veterans vouch for us in places where partisan labels are suspect.
